# Per-step fetch study: unsloth/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct

31 pauses, 42.5 teacher-forced steps per pause on average (cap 64). dNLL in nats per target token against the per-step bf16 row. Base: int2 history, block 16; block 0, the recent 64 tokens and the trailing partial block are bf16. Tool output prefilled over the int2 history without fetching (int3 row: over int3; bf16 row: over bf16).

## Checks

- bf16 row vs itself: max |dNLL| 0.0e+00
- per-step vs sdpa teacher forcing, max |log p| difference over all tokens: bf16 1.88e-01, int2 2.21e-01
- uniform int2 dNLL, sdpa batched +0.0310 vs per-step +0.0308 (max per-pause |difference| 1.1e-02)
- 42.5 s per pause on average, 21.9 min total

## Quality

Fetched = (layer, KV head, token) pairs fetched per step; distinct = distinct token positions per layer per step. Recall = share of each fetched set that is also in the oracle set of the same size, computed with the row's own current query.

Noise floor (noise_ctrl: bf16 tool-output prefill + fetch-all, exactly the bf16 row in exact arithmetic, so any dNLL is bf16 rounding in the per-step path): mean +0.0005 [95% CI -0.0009, +0.0022], s.d. over pauses 0.0045, mean |dNLL| 0.0032, max |dNLL| 0.0162; top-1 0.994 (min 0.952). Per-pause scheme differences smaller than about 0.0091 (2 s.d.) are within rounding noise.

